1:The mahjong dojos of One Han City are suitable for people of all ages as they are warm in winter and cool in summer, making them people's preferred entertainment venue in this weather.
2:But I'm not like them because I simply like to play mahjong. I've also been to dojos that don't have air conditioning, and it isn't a big deal because you'll naturally cool down after losing enough games...
3:Opposite Player
4:{character:Opposite Player}Red.
5:I pause for a moment after looking at my hand. It really isn't that easy to win with Four Concealed Triplets after all.
6:???
7:{character:???}Kan now! You're a moron if you don't Kan when you can. Go against them.
8:After I hear that familiar voice, a hand reaches out from behind me and takes the Red in the opposite player's discarded tiles and three Reds in my hand, placing them in a corner of the table...
9:{character:???}Kan!
10:player
11:{character:player}Wait!
12:{character:player}What's the point of playing an Open Kan when it's only one Han?!
13:I turn my head angrily and see Kutsuji standing behind me. He is smiling smugly, like he is very satisfied with his masterpiece just now.
14:Kutsuji
15:{character:Kutsuji}I just helped you set up something big. You'll get lots of points if you win this game.
16:I look at the Dora indicator that was just flipped over. It's a Green.
17:It's good, but...
18:{character:player}You spoke so loudly. Now everyone knows my tiles are great. Who's going to deal into my hand now?!
19:{character:Kutsuji}You can win with a Tsumo. Is that supposed to be difficult?
20:{character:player}You make it sound so easy. You get me one then!
21:I wonder if it's too late to take back what I just said because Kutsuji really did manage to help me Tsumo and win in the next turn. Although I'm sitting comfortably in first place in this Hanchan with a pile of Dora, everyone is obviously unhappy with how Kutsuji helped me win.
22:I won't be able to keep playing now.
23:I apologize to everyone and drag the culprit out of the dojo.
24:{character:player}Don't you know that a true gentleman doesn't give advice when another person is playing?
25:{character:Kutsuji}I know that.
26:{character:player}Oh I get it. You're going to tell me it doesn't apply since you're not a gentleman anyway.
27:{character:Kutsuji}Is this the legendary skill of answering for other people and leaving them with nothing to say? I learn something new from you every single time.
28:{character:player}You flatter me.
29:{character:player}You don't come to me unless you want something from me. You're here about the next part of our transaction, right?
30:{character:Kutsuji}Can't I just see you to have some fun with you? You're so coldhearted.
31:As he speaks, Kutsuji takes a red helmet from his black motorcycle and hands it to me. I glance at the blue and black helmet hanging at the front of the motorcycle and decide...
32:{character:player}I want the blue and black one.
33:{character:Kutsuji}What's your reason?
34:{character:player}It fits my cool and suave temperament better.
35:{character:player}...
35:{character:Kutsuji}...
36:{character:Kutsuji}I've never met someone who wants to use a helmet someone else has worn before instead of a new one... Fine, you're the boss. We'll do whatever you want.
37:Kutsuji mutters as he takes the blue and black helmet from the front of the motorcycle and hands it to me. It's obvious that this almost new helmet has been in good care, and the logo on it draws attention to its expensive price.
38:{character:Kutsuji}Here you go. You better wear the helmet you requested properly.
39:I sit at the back of Kutsuji's motorcycle after I receive the blue and black helmet with satisfaction and wear it. I must say that you get what you pay for. There's a reason why this helmet is expensive.
40:{character:player}Red suits you quite well. It's a good match for your arrogant temperament.
41:{character:Kutsuji}Keep praising me. I love hearing it.
42:{character:player}...I'm done. Start up your motorcycle.
43:Kutsuji is driving a modified Tiger T-REX. Although I prefer its brother in the same series, Tyrannosaurus, which is a very expensive motorcycle that appeared on my CatChat homepage from time to time.
44:Thinking of this, I feel like thanking my good friend Nadeshiko. Thanks to her influence, I'm now familiar with most motorcycles on the market, even though the extent of my familiarity with them depends on Nadeshiko's preferences because what she likes will appear on my CatChat homepage more frequently.
45:This red helmet does look better than the other one. More importantly, this helmet is the one that Nadeshiko worked for most of the year to save enough money for the deposit - the one she showed me several times with a lot of anticipation - only to have her deposit returned to her by the seller when she finally saved enough money because it was sold out!
46:The helmet in my hand is obviously brand new, and it smells like it had just been opened. I can't help feeling that it's so nice to be rich.
47:After wearing the red helmet, I sit at the back of Kutsuji's motorcycle. Kutsuji is driving a modified Tiger T-REX. Although I prefer its brother in the same series, Tyrannosaurus, which is a very expensive motorcycle that appeared on my CatChat homepage from time to time.
48:Thinking of this, I feel like thanking my good friend Nadeshiko again. Thanks to her influence, I'm now familiar with most motorcycles on the market, even though the extent of my familiarity with them depends on her preferences because the information of motorcycles she likes will appear on my CatChat homepage more frequently.
49:However, this motorcycle is living up to its name right now.
50:I feel like I'm sitting on a tiger that is running and jumping around in the forest, and I feel really insecure without a safety belt! To not fly off, I hold onto Kutsuji's jacket as hard as I can. Moreover, even the slightest sound that seems like something is tearing makes me wary of whether his jacket is breaking!
51:How can someone who is riding a motorcycle through rows of high-rise buildings make it seem like they are riding a mountain bike in a hilly area?
52:During the bumpy ride, I begin to miss the sense of security I had in the back seat of Nadeshiko's motorcycle. I start thinking to myself that I swear this is the first and last time I get on a motorcycle Kutsuji is driving.
53:We still haven't arrived at our destination after a long ride, so I resist the dizziness caused by the powerful swaying and ask Kutsuji some questions.
54:{character:player}How much longer is this ride? Why aren't we there yet?!
55:Kutsuji stops next to the road, then he stops and turns to look at me.
56:{character:Kutsuji}Oh? I thought you were having a lot of fun behind me. I was thinking of taking you around for a few more laps.
57:{character:Kutsuji}What's wrong? Is this too much for you already?
58:He is trying to goad me? I can't tolerate that, especially when I think about how he'll keep roasting me with this in the future if I shrink back at this moment.
59:{character:player}I can take more. Let's do another lap then.
60:He looks at me with raised eyebrows. Without saying anything, he starts up the engine again and repeats the route we just took... My guess is that this route must have the worst road conditions in One Han City.
61:After one lap, Kutsuji stops his motorcycle at the same spot, then he turns and looks at me.
62:{character:Kutsuji}How does it feel? Do you like it?
63:{character:Kutsuji}But... Just tell me if you can't take it anymore, and I'll take you somewhere to have a rest.
64:He's provoking me. He's definitely provoking me. I can see the naked provocation in his eyes.
65:With my bad temper, if I can stomach this, then I'll feel too embarrassed to flip the table over the next time I finish in fourth place in 20 consecutive mahjong games!
66:So, I sit up straight in the back seat and reply to Kutsuji in a steady, unperturbed, calm, and confident voice.
67:Keep going. Don't stop.
67:{character:player}Keep going. Don't stop.
68:{character:Kutsuji}I'm impressed. In that case, let me take you somewhere. It looks like the city is too small for you already.
69:Without waiting for me to ask where we'll be going, Kutsuji steps on the accelerator and speeds onto the road. Strong gusts of wind howl past my ears, drowning out the surprised cries that escape from my throat.
70:The ride isn't bumpy this time, just very fast with very high wind speeds. The scenery and other moving cars both fade quickly into the distance behind us. I, a good citizen who abides by laws and cherishes life, decide to discourage this kind of speeding behavior.
71:{character:player}You've--exceeded--the--speed--limit!
72:{character:Kutsuji}The--wind's--too--strong! I can't hear you clearly!
73:{character:player}I said--you've--exceeded--the--speed--limit!
74:{character:Kutsuji}I told you already. The--wind's--too strong! I can't hear you clearly!
75:You can never stop a person who is determined to speed. If you don't drive according to the rules, your loved ones will end up in tears.
76:When we finally stop, my body feels like it has become numb after being buffeted by the strong wind for so long. The moment I take off my helmet, I even feel like I'm not used to the outside air.
77:Kutsuji looks at me smugly, then pats the handlebar of his motorcycle. Although he hasn't said anything, I tacitly understand that he is still provoking me.
78:{character:player}Someone as upright as me will definitely fight against the forces of evil until the end, so there's no way I'll back down here.
79:{character:Kutsuji}In that case, I'll make sure I satisfy your desires.
80:We tacitly stop talking as we both get ready for the "battle". Kutsuji steps on the accelerator again, causing the motorcycle to shoot forward, and the huge inertia makes me grab his jacket and fall backward. Sigh... I forgot to remind him not to speed.
81:But he suddenly starts slowing down after advancing a short distance and stops by the side of the road.
82:{character:player}What are you doing? Are you finally going to bow down to the forces of justice?
83:{character:Kutsuji}Tsk, I'm out of gas.
84:{character:player}Out of gas?
85:{character:Kutsuji}I drove out of town yesterday and forgot to refuel my beloved motorcycle after I got back.
86:{character:Kutsuji}The main thing is that I didn't expect you would love sitting on the back seat so much.
87:{character:player}So it's my fault now? Hah!
88:I look up at the unfamiliar and desolate surroundings. We're in the suburbs now.
89:{character:player}Since you ran out of gas at such an awkward timing, do you think we will be able to get back to the city today?
90:{character:Kutsuji}You don't need to panic. I know someone around here who can give us some gas.
91:I follow Kutsuji, who is pushing the motorcycle, and we bicker the whole way as we try to blame each other for the predicament we are in. After walking for about fifteen minutes and turning at the fork in the road, I see a familiar-looking driving school.
92:What a coincidence! This is the place Nadeshiko took me to before.
93:This is obviously Kutsuji's destination. Judging from how he greets everyone here familiarly after entering, he seems to come here often as he is quite familiar with everything about the driving school.
94:The person who refuels Kutsuji's motorcycle for him happens to be the driving instructor who greeted Nadeshiko and me last time. His eyes sweep back and forth between Kutsuji and me twice, then he laughs and starts teasing me.
95:Driving Instructor
96:{character:Driving Instructor}Why aren't you here with little Nadeshiko this time?
97:{character:player}I was forced to come here this time, really.
98:{character:Driving Instructor}Haha, now that you know all the top students of our school, you have no excuse for being a bad driver in the future.
99:{character:player}Ahaha...
100:The driving instructor seems to have some misunderstanding about what it means to be a good driver. Based on what I know about Kutsuji and Nadeshiko, the only difference between them is that one bravely faces the punishment of traffic laws, while the other keeps testing the boundaries of traffic laws.
101:After refueling, Kutsuji and I bid farewell to the people here and set off for the city. This time, Kutsuji is very disciplined and drives me back honestly without speeding or taking a strange route.
102:{character:player}Why are you so familiar with the people at the driving school?
103:{character:Kutsuji}Hmm?
104:{character:player}I thought everyone at Strix taught themselves how to ride a motorcycle.
105:{character:Kutsuji}Well, you're not wrong about us being self-taught.
106:{character:Kutsuji}But we're law-abiding people. We know that it's necessary to get a driver's license first before we can ride a motorcycle. Even Strix isn't capable of issuing people driving licenses.
107:{character:player}According to the movies, aren't information dealers all experts at making false documents?
108:{character:Kutsuji}It's illegal to use false documents.
109:{character:player}Geez! The fact that you're suddenly obeying the law makes me think that you have a flexible moral bottom line.
110:{character:Kutsuji}It's good to be flexible. Anyway, if you really have the need, Strix can make you a full set of false documents.
111:{character:player}...I don't think it's likely I'll ever need to use this kind of service.
112:{character:player}Do the people at the driving school know you're the leader of Strix?
113:{character:Kutsuji}Hmm... Do you think information dealers print a stack of business cards and give them out to everyone?
114:{character:player}Oh, you don't do that?
115:I think about it for a moment. Quite a few people around me know about Strix and how to get in touch with them, which made me think they have been marketing themselves well.
116:{character:player}...I don't have any more questions. You can drive quietly now, and please take me to the destination safely, thank you.
117:{character:Kutsuji}Hah!
118:After Kutsuji returns to the urban area, he takes me to a teahouse near Countless Springs. I'm quite familiar with the scenery in these parts now since I've been here twice recently. Kutsuji leads me into the teahouse from the back door and goes straight to a private room on the second floor.
119:{character:player}Why did you suddenly want to come here?
120:{character:Kutsuji}It's to show you a brilliant performance, of course.
121:I sit by the window and immediately understand what he is referring to when I look out the window. The window of this private room faces the street where the main entrance of the teahouse is located, and a grand geisha parade is taking place right now.
122:{character:Kutsuji}Every once in a while, Countless Springs selects an auspicious day for the most popular geisha to wear her exclusive costume. She will walk from the entrance of Countless Springs to the end of the street and then return to Countless Springs. This is called the geisha parade.
123:{character:Kutsuji}One reason it is held is to highlight the unparalleled beauty of Countless Springs's geisha. Another reason is that Countless Springs owns all the businesses here, and only the most popular geisha is qualified to manage Countless Springs and take over these businesses.
124:{character:Kutsuji}So this parade also symbolizes an inspection tour of their own businesses and is a demonstration of their sovereignty.
125:{character:Kutsuji}Kurone Toujou has been the manager of Countless Springs ever since she conquered everyone with her talent and beauty when she was still a young girl more than ten years ago.
126:{character:Kutsuji}She is also the geisha who is in charge of the geisha parade every time it is held now.
127:I watch the parade while leaning against the window and listening to Kutsuji's explanation. In the middle of the crowd is a splendidly-dressed woman, but I can't see her appearance clearly due to the distance and because she is wearing a veil that seems to be made of a beaded curtain. Kutsuji casually taps the window frame and gives me a reminder.
128:{character:Kutsuji}That's Kurone Toujou.
129:The same mistake shouldn't be made more than three times, and you shouldn't start playing mahjong from the North. My principle is to be as flexible as an inchworm. As I no longer want to experience an unhealthy recreational activity such as a high-speed drive through One Han City, I choose to back down for now.
130:Surprisingly, Kutsuji doesn't take the chance to tease me further. Instead, he smiles and taps the helmet in my hand.
131:{character:Kutsuji}Put it back on. I'll take you for a real drive now.
132:I dubiously sit back on the back seat of his motorcycle. This time, Kutsuji drives at an obviously slower speed, and the breeze blowing on my exposed skin feels cool and pleasant.
133:But I start to feel the motorcycle slowing down before long. Finally, we stop by the side of the road.
134:{character:player}What's wrong?
135:He falls silent for a few seconds before turning to look at me.
136:{character:Kutsuji}I'm out of gas.
137:After gloating at his misfortune for 30 seconds, I look around us and suddenly realize that we're in the suburbs and have no way to get back.
138:The person who refuels Kutsuji's motorcycle for him happens to be the driving instructor who greeted Nadeshiko and me last time. His eyes sweep back and forth between Kutsuji and me twice, then he laughs and starts teasing me.
139:After refueling, Kutsuji and I bid farewell to the people here and set off for the city.
140:{character:Kutsuji}Every once in a while, Countless Springs selects an auspicious day for the most popular geisha to wear her exclusive costume. She will walk from the entrance of Countless Springs to the end of the street and then return to Countless Springs. This is called the geisha parade.
141:{character:Kutsuji}She is also the geisha who is in charge of the geisha parade every time it is held now.
142:{character:player}Don't tell me you're trying to let me experience what it's like to go on a motorcycle ride that feels like a roller coaster ride.
143:{character:Kutsuji}That's a rude analogy. No roller coaster ride is as exciting as a ride on the back seat of my motorcycle.
144:{character:Kutsuji}To me, the physical sensation of a roller coaster is at best like watching "Autobots 6" in 4D. The seat will shake a few times, and I'll see some effects through the 3D glasses.
145:{character:Kutsuji}If you don't believe me, I can take you out for another two laps so you can really feel it.
146:The sensible side of me tells me there's no need to experience something like that. There are always things in life that we insist on meaninglessly even though they don't bring us substantial benefits.
147:For example, winning a dare if you throw a piece of chalk at the head of the class teacher, having everyone admit that you're the greatest among everyone present if you dare to lick an iron railing in winter, or winning people's respect if you dare to say: "I don't care about what you think because I only care about what I think" loudly to your boss at next week's regular meeting...
148:Someone who is mentally mature like me will never be provoked into doing something that brings no real benefits a second time.
149:{character:player}Thanks but no thanks.
150:{character:player}I think we should find a place to finish our transaction first.
151:{character:Kutsuji}Sigh, what a shame. In that case, sit tight while I take you somewhere.
152:{character:player}Where are we going?
153:{character:Kutsuji}You'll find out when we get there.
154:After that, we experienced the same familiar scenery from before, except this time it feels like we are experiencing it in reverse. The only difference is that one of the streets we passed by was now wet, as if it had just rained in this area.
155:As the road is slippery, Kutsuji drives steadily after that because he cares about his own life even if he doesn't care about mine. The breeze after the rain feels cool on my skin and even feels a little comfortable.
156:After so many twists and turns, I didn't expect our destination to be a teahouse diagonally opposite Countless Springs. I'm quite familiar with the scenery in these parts now since I've been here twice recently. Kutsuji leads me into the teahouse from the back door and goes straight to a private room on the second floor.
157:{character:Kutsuji}I've brought you here to show you a brilliant performance.
158:{character:Kutsuji}This is the best place to watch the performance. Whenever there's a performance, reserving this spot is as difficult as winning that auction last time.
159:I sit by the window and look out the window. The window of this private room faces the street where the main entrance of the teahouse is located, and it is densely packed with approximately as many people as the day of the auction for the cut flowers.
160:{character:Kutsuji}Have you heard of the geisha parade before?
161:{character:player}Yes.
162:{character:Kutsuji}Countless Springs also has a custom like that. Every once in a while, it selects an auspicious day for the most popular geisha to wear her exclusive costume. She will walk from the entrance of Countless Springs to the end of the street and then return to Countless Springs. This is called the geisha parade.
163:After he finishes talking, I see the doors of Countless Springs open amidst loud cheering.
164:Several men wearing the same outfit walk out holding wooden signs in their hands and stand on both sides of the road. On the wooden signs are the emblem of Countless Springs and some words, but the words are too small for me to read them clearly.
165:Immediately after that, six girls wearing exquisite costumes line up on both sides, holding flower baskets as they exit the door in two lines. As they walk, they grab flowers in their baskets and throw them to their side, and the flowers land on the ground in the path between them.
166:Accompanied by the sound of rhythmic drums and music, I see a foot wearing white socks and high clogs stick out from the door, drawing a half-moon arc before hiding behind the door again, like a playful goldfish wagging its tail in the air after jumping out of the water.
167:After this repeats several times, a splendidly-dressed woman exits the door and walks slowly along the flower-paved road, maintaining a goldfish-like pace.
168:Due to the distance and because she is wearing a veil that seems to be made of a beaded curtain, I can't see her appearance clearly. Kutsuji casually taps the window frame and gives me a reminder.
169:Although I can see that he is provoking me, Kutsuji's driving skills are too much for me.
170:{character:player}I have motion sickness.
171:{character:Kutsuji}Oh... what a shame.
172:{character:Kutsuji}In that case, let's go to our destination.
173:{character:Kutsuji}You'll find out when we get there.
174:A thundershower starts just as we turn around to drive back. I remember seeing a blue rainstorm warning in the morning, but I was in the dojo at that time and never thought it would be relevant to me.
175:The torrential rain starts suddenly, drenching me like a bucket of water over my head. However, the outrageous thing is that nothing happened to Kutsuji, who is right in front of me. There is only less than ten centimeters between us, but the rain curtain has separated us into two different worlds.
176:To avoid getting rained on as much as possible, I press my body toward him and try to get as much of my head out of the rain curtain as possible. I remember a monkey I saw at the zoo in the past and think I look like that monkey after it stumbled into a ditch and was about to drown... Blergh! It's insulting to think about myself in that way.
177:{character:Kutsuji}I have something to say.
178:{character:Kutsuji}Can you stay away from me? Don't lean against me, you've gotten my back all wet.
179:{character:player}Drive faster then. Can't you see the rain right behind us?!
180:{character:Kutsuji}Hey... This is an urban area. My license will be suspended if I speed here.
181:{character:player}It doesn't matter since it's not my license anyway.
182:The pouring rain follows us all the way until we pass through an underground tunnel and reach the other side. I look at my fully drenched self and at Kutsuji, who is only wet around the back area, then I squint my eyes.
183:{character:player}You must have done that on purpose.
184:{character:Kutsuji}I'm innocent. I'm sure you know that One Han City is famous for its unpredictable weather. I didn't expect this to happen at all.
185:{character:Kutsuji}All I can say is that you're really special after all. I won't be surprised no matter what miracle happens to you now.
186:Kutsuji comforts me while he drives. When we finally stop, I realize that we're at the entrance of Chaque Jour.
187:{character:Kutsuji}To make amends, you can pick any outfit you want, and I'll give it to you for free as an apology.
188:I clean my hands quickly after entering the store and then start looking through the clothes. I decide to forgive him after looking at the price tags. After all, there's no bad blood between good partners.
189:After I get dressed and follow Kutsuji to the destination he mentioned, I realize that it is a teahouse diagonally opposite Countless Springs. I'm quite familiar with the scenery in these parts now since I've been here twice recently. Kutsuji leads me into the teahouse from the back door and goes straight to a private room on the second floor.
190:I sit by the window and look out the window. The window of this private room faces the street where the main entrance of the teahouse is located, and it is densely packed with approximately as many people as the day of the auction for the cut flowers. However, the flow of people has been blocked off by cordons on both sides of the street, leaving the middle of the street vacant. Meanwhile, some staff wearing the uniform of Countless Springs are monitoring the situation closely.
191:Kutsuji casually spins the plate of snacks in front of him and seems lost in thought. After a while, he looks up at me and starts explaining the situation.
192:{character:player}Huh? Doesn't that mean today is that auspicious day?
193:{character:Kutsuji}You're so smart.
194:{character:Kutsuji}You deserve a reward for getting it right. Your reward will be this plate of a snack called "cardamom."
195:As he speaks, he decisively pushes the plate of snacks he has been spinning around for a while toward me. At the same time, the faint fragrance of durian wafts over, telling me exactly what this snack tastes like.
196:As expected of an information dealer. He even knows that I like durian. But come to think of it, they've investigated me thoroughly, and my love for durian isn't a secret at all.
197:I receive a "cardamom" from Kutsuji and take a bite. The unique sweetness of durian fills my mouth instantly. This snack is filled with chunks of durian flesh, which has an ice cream-like texture after chilling. One bite of this snack is enough to fill a person with satisfaction and happiness. It is a treasure in this world.
198:I am filled with satisfaction after eating two pieces in a row. When I look up and see Kutsuji deliberately keeping his distance from me, as well as the look of disbelief on his face, I suddenly realize something.
199:{character:player}You don't eat durian?
200:{character:Kutsuji}I don't eat it... I have no idea how anyone can like this type of thing.
201:{character:player}What? Durian is so tasty!
202:{character:Kutsuji}Tsk...
203:{character:Kutsuji}Ning tricked me into taking a bite when I was little... It tasted like a scallion pancake that had gone bad for a week.
204:{character:player}Who's "Ning"?
205:{character:Kutsuji}She's the person who raised me.
206:{character:player}Is she also a member of Strix?
207:{character:Kutsuji}Yes and no.
208:{character:player}Oh, you should try some now then. I think there might have been something wrong with the piece you ate back then.
209:{character:Kutsuji}That won't be necessary.
210:{character:Kutsuji}Oh and I'm not the only one who doesn't eat it. Nobody in Strix eats durian.
211:Suddenly, Kutsuji moves closer to me while pinching his nose and speaks in a low voice.
212:{character:Kutsuji}There's something you must remember.
213:{character:Kutsuji}It's a serious crime to eat durian inside Strix. Something terrible will happen.
214:{character:player}Is there some sort of punishment?
215:He smiles strangely. It is a smile that feels... very threatening.
216:{character:Kutsuji}You're welcome to find out.
217:{character:player}No... It's not like I'll get anything even if I do it.
218:After listening to Kutsuji's words, the "cardamom" on the plate is no longer appetizing to me, so I push the plate slightly further away from me.
219:{character:player}Forget it. Let's change the subject and talk about the next part of our transaction.
220:{character:Kutsuji}Speaking of our transaction, the parade is about to start. It won't be too late to tell you after we finish watching the parade.
221:I follow his gaze and look downstairs, only to realize that it had become quiet downstairs at some point. Everyone stops making noise and looks at the entrance of Countless Springs expectantly.
222:When the time on my phone reaches the hour on the dot, the doors of Countless Springs opens amidst a burst of loud cheering.
223:Accompanied by the sound of rhythmic drums and music, I see a foot wearing white socks and high clogs stick out from the door, drawing a half-moon arc before hiding behind the door again, like a playful goldfish wagging its tail in the air after jumping out of the water.
224:I push the plate back to Kutsuji expressionlessly. I won't eat it. I would starve to death today or jump off from the second floor before I take a single bite.
225:To my surprise, Kutsuji pauses for a moment before pushing it back to me. A piece of the snack splits off and falls on the plate as we keep pushing it back and forth... making the smell of durian even more potent.
226:{character:Kutsuji}It's not good to waste food.
227:{character:player}Then you shouldn't waste any.
228:When I push the plate back to him again, I notice that he is pushing the edge of the plate firmly with his fingers while holding his chin with his other hand and pretending to look away.
229:{character:player}Is it possible that you... don't eat durian?
230:{character:Kutsuji}I don't eat it.
231:{character:player}Why did you order it then if you don't eat it?
232:{character:Kutsuji}Who would have known that this traditional teahouse would follow the trend and also start making durian snacks... They even gave it a name that has nothing to do with durian.
233:{character:player}Oh, I didn't expect there to be something an information dealer doesn't know.
234:Kutsuji's expression gradually becomes stiff after hearing my words. It's obvious that even he didn't realize he would make such a mistake. However, he is a leader who has been through a lot, so it doesn't take him long to become his usual carefree self again.
235:{character:Kutsuji}It doesn't matter. It's not too late to collect this piece of information today.
236:{character:Kutsuji}In view of your contribution, I'll mark down first-class merit for you.
237:{character:player}I'm not a member of Strix. I don't need this first-class merit...
238:{character:player}But I won't say no if you insist on giving it to me. It'll be even better if I can redeem it for something more practical.
239:{character:Kutsuji}Something practical... Then I'll make an exception and allow you to waste food.
240:After that, Kutsuji turns and calls a waiter to remove this plate of snacks and replace it with a different-flavored snack.
241:{character:player}That's it? Aren't you afraid I'll tell others that you don't eat durian?
242:{character:Kutsuji}Haha, you don't need to threaten me. You can't move me with force or persuasion, and I only engage in profitable transactions.
243:{character:player}Oh, that's right. Speaking of which, don't you think it's time we got on with the rest of the transaction?
244:{character:Kutsuji}There's no rush. The parade is about to start. It won't be too late to take our time chatting after we finish watching the parade.
245:Kutsuji taps the window frame rhythmically along with the music below and seems immersed in the performance. When Kurone Toujou walks directly below us, he suddenly turns his head to look at me.
246:{character:Kutsuji}I'm thinking of telling you something before we continue with the transaction.
247:{character:player}What is it?
248:{character:Kutsuji}I'm guessing that you must want to know why I got you to participate in the auction and everything else that happened after that, right?
249:{character:player}Yeah, because I felt like I didn't get any particularly valuable information.
250:{character:Kutsuji}No, the fact that you went is already a piece of valuable information.
251:{character:player}What do you mean?
252:{character:Kutsuji}What if I told you that you would be able to meet Kurone Toujou no matter which flower arrangement you managed to get?
253:{character:player}Is it because all three flower arrangements are hers?
254:{character:Kutsuji}No, it's because she wants to meet you.
255:{character:player}Huh?
256:{character:Kutsuji}At first, I made this guess based on the information I gathered, but your actions afterward helped me verify my guess.
257:Kutsuji's words make the question mark in my head grow larger. Based on my interaction with Kurone Toujou, I can't figure out why she would want to actively approach me.
258:{character:Kutsuji}Our previous transaction is still valid, but I can change its terms for you. From now on, you have two options.
259:{character:Kutsuji}Your first option is to ask me about Ciri like we agreed, and I will tell you what she's been up to recently.
260:{character:Kutsuji}Your second option is to ask me about Kurone Toujou for yourself, and I will tell you selected pieces of information that are useful to you.
261:{character:Kutsuji}I'll give you some time to think it over. I hope you'll make the decision that satisfies your true inner needs.
262:I think deeply for a moment after hearing Kutsuji's words. Emotionally and rationally, I should ask him about Ciri's matters since that was why I approached him in the first place and the matter I was entrusted with.
263:On the other hand, I really want to know Kurone Toujou's reason for doing that. Now that I think about it, there seems to be a deeper layer of meaning to the things we talked about on that day. Some things that I consider ordinary and mundane might not be as simple as I thought.
264:I think about it for a long time but have difficulty deciding. Sara and Ryan's worried expressions appear in my head one after the other, but I can hear Kurone Toujou's soft and pleasant voice in the background.
265:{character:Kutsuji}You know, you can be a little selfish sometimes. No one would blame you for that.
266:In that case, my decision is...
267:{character:player}I've decided. I want to know more about Kurone Toujou... Or rather, I want to know more about me.
268:Kutsuji doesn't seem surprised by my decision. He laughs and then motions for me to watch Kurone Toujou carefully.
269:{character:Kutsuji}Do you notice anything different about Kurone Toujou today compared with when you met her a few days ago?
270:His question catches me off guard. To be honest, I can only see her figure vaguely from this distance. Moreover, when I met Kurone Toujou the other day, there was a screen between us when we chatted, so I don't have enough information to make a comparison.
271:But if I had to comment on this, there are still some differences.
272:The Kurone Toujou who is parading through the street right now seems to only have one tail, but I seem to remember seeing several tails waving around behind the screen that day.
273:{character:player}My eyes might have been playing tricks on me, but I have a strong feeling that Kurone Toujou had more than one tail that day. However... there was a screen between us, so what I saw might have been the shadows of other decorations.
274:Kutsuji looks very calm and composed when he hears what I say, as if he isn't surprised at all.
275:{character:Kutsuji}Have you heard the legend of the nine-tailed fox?
276:{character:player}It depends on which version you're referring to. There are so many different stories about a legendary mythical creature like the nine-tailed fox.
277:{character:player}The tales about her range from her being a demoness that brings calamity to countries to her being a ninjutsu energy source. I could talk about her for more than one day if you don't define the range.
278:{character:Kutsuji}Whoa, you're more knowledgeable than I expected. Now I'm getting more and more curious about your browser history. You should show me when you have time.
279:I recall my recent searches and think that there's no way I will show them to him... Wait, what I searched doesn't matter at all. The question is, why should I show him my browser history in the first place?!
280:{character:player}No, I refuse.
281:{character:Kutsuji}Fine, it doesn't matter. I'll get an opportunity one day.
282:{character:Kutsuji}The specific version I'm referring to is One Han City's legend of the nine-tailed fox. Have you heard this version before?
283:{character:player}No, not that one. I didn't even know One Han City had its own version.
284:{character:Kutsuji}Actually, there has always been a group of people in One Han City who firmly believe that the nine-tailed fox in the legends exists. They created a secret organization for the nine-tailed fox and started worshipping her.
285:{character:Kutsuji}In the version of the legend they believe in, the nine-tailed fox really is a demoness who brings calamity to countries, but only because human beings have committed an unforgivable crime.
286:{character:Kutsuji}The nine-tailed fox is resurrected whenever an era changes to subvert the old era and lead its followers to usher in a new era.
287:{character:player}So are you saying that Kurone Toujou is the nine-tailed fox?
288:{character:Kutsuji}I'm not sure. She may or may not. Kurone Toujou and the legendary nine-tailed fox do share some traits, but they are not exactly the same.
289:{character:player}Haha, don't tell me she hasn't fully evolved yet and is in an incomplete form.
290:{character:Kutsuji}You might be right.
291:I look at the serious look on Kutsuji's face. When I realize that he doesn't seem to be joking, the smile freezes on my face. If this is true and the nine-tailed fox is watching me... I can't even imagine what will happen next.
292:{character:player}Am I in any danger?
293:Upon hearing this, Kutsuji fumbles through the pocket of his coat for a long time before pulling out a card and handing it to me. I take a look at it nervously and see that it is an introduction of Strix's business scope... For a while, I'm lost for words and don't know what I should complain about first.
294:{character:Kutsuji}From the moment you chose to ask about Kurone Toujou, the transaction we just had counts as the first transaction, and there will be a second or third transaction after that. In short, the doors of Strix will always be open to you in the future.
295:I look at him in response to his words and note that he is looking at me with a gentle smile, without showing any signs of ridiculing or teasing me. Out of the corner of my eye, I see Kurone Toujou walk slowly on the street behind him. Her gorgeous figure is now a huge mystery in my eyes.
296:I know that I'll also become part of the mystery when Kutsuji and I reach this kind of agreement. I might eventually learn the truth after a painstaking investigation, or I might be swallowed by the mystery due to my incompetence.
297:"One Han City isn't as calm as I think." Many people have told me this. Now, it's up to me to see just how turbulent it is for myself.
298:I put the card in my bag and nod at Kutsuji.
299:He hands me a cup he has filled with tea, then he raises another cup and clinks it against my cup.
300:{character:Kutsuji}Let's gaze into the abyss together.
301:{character:player}I've decided. I want to know more about Ciri.
302:{character:Kutsuji}I'll tell you then since you've made up your mind. If what you and Soul want to know is why Ciri has been visiting Countless Springs frequently recently, it's because a syndicate that mainly resells rare wild animals appeared in One Han City recently. Kurone Toujou happened to save a red-crowned crane they were trafficking and handed it to Ciri.
303:{character:Kutsuji}You people should know Ciri better than me. Probably due to her background as a well-known wildlife conservationist in One Han City, she has been investigating this incident and trying to rescue these animals recently.
304:{character:Kutsuji}As for the issue of money... Haha, that's what the members of Soul are most concerned about. About how Ciri has the money to buy tickets to Countless Springs, the answer is Kurone Toujou gave her an entry pass for some reason, which means she can enter Countless Springs for free.
305:{character:player}That's it?
306:{character:Kutsuji}That's it.
307:I didn't expect the answer Kutsuji gave me at all, but it also makes perfect sense when I think about it.
308:The geisha parade has ended by the time I finish chatting with Kutsuji about this, so I said goodbye to him and went directly to Soul to tell Sara what has happened.
309:Sara
310:{character:Sara}Oh, when I saw that you hadn't been coming to watch our performances, I guessed that you were taking independent action, but I didn't expect to be right.
311:{character:player}Anyway, it's good that this incident has a happy ending.
312:{character:player}So please forgive me for taking independent action. Please also hide this from Ryan, or else he'll be unhappy for a while.
313:{character:Sara}You... You and Ciri are very similar to some extent.
314:{character:player}Huh?
315:{character:Sara}You both like to take on the burden of other people's affairs and do so much for others, yet you never ask others for anything in return.
316:{character:player}I just want to do everything I can to help you guys because you're important friends to me.
317:{character:Sara}Please promise me that you'll come to me for help if you ever encounter any problems in the future. I want you to be able to rely on me too.
318:{character:Sara}Instead of doing everything on your own, I prefer it if you are more willing to trouble us. I believe the other members of Soul think the same way.
319:{character:Sara}This is because we see you as a member of our family and a part of Soul.
320:{character:player}Okay, I will. Thank you, Sara.
321:I stay behind and have dinner with everyone in Soul that night. I can see that Sara is in a good mood tonight. She even takes her shoes off and starts dancing rhythmically next to the bonfire amidst everyone's cheering.
322:Ciri
323:{character:Ciri}{var:player_nickname}, thanks for everything this time.
324:Ciri came over to me when I wasn't paying attention and thanked me softly. She tells me that Sara helped her explain everything to the other members of Soul, and everyone also apologized to her for how they had been acting recently.
325:{character:Ciri}Actually, they didn't need to apologize to me because this incident isn't anyone's fault... The reason why I didn't tell them in the beginning is that I didn't want to be a burden to everyone because of something I wanted to do personally. I didn't expect to create such a big misunderstanding.
326:{character:Ciri}I even caused you and Sara to worry about me. If you didn't help out this time, this matter might have escalated so much that I can't deal with it. No matter what, I have to thank you properly and express my gratitude.
327:I take the drink she hands me and clink glasses with her. The drink seems to be a special drink that is cool and delicious with a herbal fragrance.
328:I look up at the moon hanging in the sky and note that the moon is almost full. It won't be long until the Mid-Autumn Festival arrives again.
329:It's so nice when everyone is together under the full moon.
330:{character:player}In that case, why don't you just tell me both things?
331:{character:Kutsuji}Haha, I never do business at a loss. You've only done one task for me, so there's no reason why you should receive two rewards.
332:After he finishes speaking, he turns to look at Kurone Toujou downstairs. I don't know what to say, so I follow suit and watch the performance below us. After a while, Kutsuji speaks softly and emotionlessly next to me.
333:{character:Kutsuji}In One Han City, knowing more isn't necessarily better. There's a saying... Oh yes, with great power comes great responsibility.
334:{character:Kutsuji}Once you know certain things, you won't be able to ignore them.
335:{character:Kutsuji}Isn't it better to just be a Jyanshi who plays mahjong happily every day? Those who are curious about the abyss will be swallowed by it sooner or later.
336:After saying this, he turns to look at me and takes out a copper coin from his trouser pocket.
337:{character:Kutsuji}I'll give you one last chance to decide. If you don't, I'll flip this copper coin and let it decide for you. Heads is Ciri, and tails is Kurone Toujou.
338:It's a little irresponsible to leave something this important to a copper coin. I'll make my own decision.
339:During a game
340:Two minutes later
341:I want the blue and black helmet
343:I want the red helmet
344:A Jyanshi can never give up. Let's do another lap.
345:The most important thing is to stay alive. That's enough.
346:It's meaningless to persist about some things. I want to get off.
347:Are you satisfied with just that? How typical!
348:You win.
349:
350:Who can say no to durian? Of course I'll take it.
351:No way! Who on earth adds durian to a snack?
352:I want to know more about Kurone Toujou.
353:I want to know more about Ciri.
354:Why can't you tell me both things?
